  "released": "2026-08-14",
  "changelog": "v166: decisions feed the loop (ADR 0009) \u2014 the review surface's owner decisions become real training signal instead of being archived unread. Fixed a field-overwrite defect: candidates-update --reason (and the hosted platform's defer/dismiss) used to clobber the generator's own provenance reason in place; it now writes a separate decision_reason field, so both survive and both render (CLI detail view, the Review lane's history groups). The most recent owner decisions (DISMISSED/DEFERRED/PROMOTED, human-only) now feed BOTH generation prompts as an \"Owner Judgment Signals\" block (question_judgment.build_decision_context) \u2014 candidates matching the pattern of recent dismissals are told not to be re-proposed. Wires ADR 0007's declared-but-unwired weekly RUBRIC-EDIT: a new judgment-update command reads the week's decisions plus quality-profile bucket movements, calls the role.planner tier (keyless machines emit an agent task instead), and applies AT MOST one bounded, evidence-cited amendment to state/question_judgment/learned.md \u2014 never a rewrite, never a deterministic invention, with a hard per-entry character cap and mechanical oldest-entry compaction when the file grows past its own cap. A cursor file makes a same-week re-run a no-op. Runs weekly right after the quality-profile update, before candidate auto-promotion. A --recalibrate variant swaps the delta for the full decision ledger (manual only, quarterly cadence, no scheduler wiring yet). See ADR 0009; a follow-up (lifehug/lifehug#148) tracks whether the numeric quality score should also calibrate on this signal.",
